ainer for screen readers"],[316,"`aria-label=\"Close\"` on the built-in close button"],[236,"`aria-labelledby` associates the visible label when the `label` prop is provided"],[779,"`aria-labelledby` associates the visible label when the `label` prop is provided"],[198,"`aria-required` when selection is required"],[892,"`aria-required` when selection is required"],[234,"`aria-valuemin` and `aria-valuemax` define the range (default `0`–`100`)"],[777,"`aria-valuemin` and `aria-valuemax` define the range (default `0`–`100`)"],[776,"`aria-valuenow` reflects the current value"],[233,"`aria-valuenow` reflects the current value (clamped to 0–100)"],[778,"`aria-valuetext` provides a formatted string (e.g. `\"60%\"`)"],[235,"`aria-valuetext` provides a formatted string (e.g. `\"60%\"`) via `Intl.NumberFormat`; the same string is rendered inside the circle. Override the text with the `aria-valuetext` prop, or control formatting with `formatOptions`"],[1540,"`Box` is a polymorphic layout component that renders as any HTML element or custom component via the `as` prop. It provides consistent spacing, elevation, rounding, and self-alignment within flex or grid containers."],[103,"`Calendar` values are `CalendarDate` objects. Import the date primitives you need from the `@godaddy/antares/date` subpath:"],[1509,"`colorIndex` pins each series to a palette color. Any series can use any index,\nindependently — here two pairs each share an index so an actual line and its\ndashed forecast read as the same color, distinguished only by line style."],[811,"`currentStep` is the single source of truth for the timeline. Omit it for a not-yet-started flow where every step is `future`; pass the step count for a fully completed flow where every step is `past`."],[491,"`data-color`: Applied when color prop is set"],[494,"`data-flip`: Applied when flip prop is set (\"horizontal\" or \"vertical\")"],[490,"`data-icon`: The icon name (always present)"],[492,"`data-loading`: Applied during icon loading from CDN"],[493,"`data-mode`: Applied when mode prop is set (e.g., \"sprite\")"],[495,"`data-rotate`: Applied when rotate prop is set (90, 180, or 270)"],[1089,"`data-selected`, `data-hovered`, `data-pressed`, `data-focused`, `data-focus-visible`, `data-disabled`, `data-readonly`, `data-invalid`, `data-required`, `data-size`"],[257,"`DatePicker` (single) and `DateRangePicker` (range): a read-only formatted date label; the whole field opens a calendar popover"],[297,"`DrawerTrigger` is the composition helper: it wraps a trigger button and a `<Drawer>`, handling open state and `aria-controls` linkage automatically. Based on RAC `DialogTrigger`."],[386,"`Enter` / `Space`"],[567,"`Enter` / `Space`"],[310,"`Escape`"],[699,"`Escape`"],[347,"`FieldGroup` is purely presentational — it renders the styled `Group` and holds no React Aria context. The surrounding field wires value, disabled, and validation state into its controls."],[348,"`FieldGroup` rounds its outer corners from DOM order: the group's CSS rounds the start corners of its **first child** and the end corners of its **last child**, so controls are seamless inside and rounded only at the box edges. Author children in visual order and the rounding follows — no per-control positioning prop. A lone control (a TextField input, a Select trigger) is both first and last, so it rounds both edges. The rules are RTL-safe (they use logical `start`/`end` corners)."],[344,"`FieldLabel`, `FieldDescription`, and `FieldError` each render `null` when they have no content, so callers pass `label` / `description` / `errorMessage` straight through without guarding."],[412,"`FileTrigger` adds no visuals or ARIA of its own — accessibility comes from the pressable child you provide. Use a component with an accessible name (e.g. an Antares `Button` with clear label text) so assistive technology announces the action. The underlying `<input>` is visually hidden but remains operable by keyboard through the child's press behavior."],[1577,"`Flex` is a one-dimensional layout component for arranging children in rows or columns with alignment and spacing control. It extends `Box`, inheriting all `Box` capabilities (padding, elevation, rounding, self-alignment, and polymorphic `as` prop)."],[499,"`focusable=\"false\"`: Prevents keyboard focus"],[270,"`formatOptions` accepts any `Intl.DateTimeFormatOptions` (e.g. `{ dateStyle: 'short' }`, `{ month: 'long', year: 'numeric' }`). `placeholder` sets the empty-state text."],[1615,"`Grid` is a two-dimensional CSS Grid layout component for complex grid-based layouts. It extends `Box`, inheriting all `Box` capabilities (padding, elevation, rounding, self-alignment, and polymorphic `as` prop)."],[193,"`horizontal`: Arranges checkboxes in a horizontal row"],[555,"`InlineDrawerPanel` is the collapsible content for the accordion pattern — a thin wrapper over RAC `DisclosurePanel` that hides when collapsed. The trigger is any component you slot in with `slot=\"trigger\"` — there's no dedicated trigger component."],[1492,"`legendPosition` puts the legend above or below the plot, or hides it with `null`. Multi-series charts get a bottom legend by default."],[1546,"`lg` - Large spacing"],[639,"`ListBox` requires either `aria-label` or `aria-labelledby`. For a labeled, popover-style picker, prefer `Select`."],[1545,"`md` - Medium spacing"],[608,"`MenuTrigger` exposes its open state via `isOpen`/`onOpenChange`,\nwhich can be used to drive the rotation of a chevron icon."],[101,"`minValue` / `maxValue` bounds and `isDateUnavailable` per-day disabling"],[260,"`minValue` / `maxValue` bounds and `isDateUnavailable` per-day disabling"],[810,"`orientation` switches between `horizontal` (accent bar on top) and `vertical` (accent bar on the leading edge)."],[1352,"`orientation=\"horizontal\"` swaps the axes: categories run down the side and values across the bottom. Reach for it when the labels are long or the chart is really a ranking."],[299,"`overlay` elevation panel over a dimmed backdrop, matching `Modal`"],[575,"`placement` does not flip in RTL; the side is decided by document/flex order."],[558,"`placement` selects the collapse axis (`left`/`right` → width, `top`/`bottom` → height)"],[561,"`prefers-reduced-motion` support"],[1511,"`renderTooltip` example combining a pair of series. Each pair shares a `colorIndex`\n(solid actual + dashed forecast); hovering either line shows the percent change of\nthe forecast against the actual for that pair, wrapped in the default styled popover."],[1512,"`renderTooltip` example styled as a period-over-period comparison card. Paired series\n(solid current period + dashed previous period) share a `colorIndex`; hovering either\nline shows both dated values and the percent change, wrapped in the default popover."],[1510,"`renderTooltip` lets you render a fully custom tooltip and know which curve is\nhovered. Paired series share a `colorIndex`; hovering either line shows a\ntooltip specific to that line, wrapped in the default styled popover."],[701,"`role=\"dialog\"` is applied automatically by the underlying React Aria `Dialog`"],[314,"`role=\"dialog\"` with `aria-modal=\"true\"` on the drawer panel (via RAC Modal)"],[498,"`role=\"img\"`: When title prop is provided"],[497,"`role=\"presentation\"`: For decorative icons"],[232,"`role=\"progressbar\"` on the container"],[775,"`role=\"progressbar\"` on the container"],[889,"`role=\"radio\"` on each option"],[1013,"`role=\"radio\"` on each segment"],[888,"`role=\"radiogroup\"` on the container"],[1012,"`role=\"radiogroup\"` on the container"],[1240,"`selectionMode=\"multiple\"` → `role=\"toolbar\"` on container, `role=\"button\"` + `aria-pressed` per item"],[1239,"`selectionMode=\"single\"` → `role=\"radiogroup\"` on container, `role=\"radio\"` + `aria-checked` per item"],[697,"`Shift + Tab`"],[614,"`size` controls item density. Shown here as two standalone menus so both\nsizes are visible at once; in practice you set `size` on the `Menu` inside a\n`MenuT